# `rates::vasicek_paths`

Simulates paths of the Vasicek short rate `dr = κ(θ − r)dt + σ dW`.

## Signature

```cpp
rates::RatePaths rates::vasicek_paths(std::int64_t steps, std::int64_t paths, double dt, const rates::VasicekParams &params, const rates::SimOptions &options, pluss::Config cfg = {}, std::uint64_t seed = 0);
rates::RatePaths rates::vasicek_paths(std::int64_t steps, std::int64_t paths, double dt, const rates::VasicekParams &params, pluss::Config cfg = {}, std::uint64_t seed = 0);
```

## What It Does

Steps `steps` times of length `dt` from `r0` and returns the rate at every date for every path as a [`RatePaths`](RatePaths.md). The scheme is chosen in the options: with `Scheme::Transition` the step is exact for any `dt`, with `Euler` it has a discretisation error of order `dt`. The two signatures differ in where the random-number settings come from: the first takes a full [`SimOptions`](SimOptions.md), the second uses the defaults with the given `seed`.

## Parameters

`std::int64_t steps`
: Number of time steps, positive.

`std::int64_t paths`
: Number of paths, positive.

`double dt`
: Step length in years, positive and finite.

`const rates::VasicekParams &params`
: The model.

`const rates::SimOptions &options`
: Scheme, random numbers, layout, seed (first form).

`pluss::Config cfg`
: Device (and pinned memory) of the result; the type is Float64.

`std::uint64_t seed`
: Seed of the pseudo-random stream in the second form (the first reads `options.seed`).

## Returns

A [`RatePaths`](RatePaths.md).

## Errors

- A non-positive `steps`, `paths` or `dt`, invalid parameters, or invalid options throw (`pluss::Error`).

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The distribution at maturity. With the exact scheme, `r_T` is Gaussian with mean `θ + (r₀ − θ)e^{−κT}` and variance `σ²(1 − e^{−2κT})/(2κ)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <cmath>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace rt = fin::rates;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const rt::VasicekParams p{.kappa = 0.7, .theta = 0.03, .sigma = 0.01, .r0 = 0.06};
  rt::SimOptions options;
  options.scheme = rt::Scheme::Transition;
  options.seed = 3;
  const Series rT = rt::vasicek_paths(4, 100000, 0.5, p, options).rate.select(0, 4);
  out.writeln("mean", rT.mean().item<double>(), "exact", 0.03 + 0.03 * std::exp(-0.7 * 2.0));
  out.writeln("sd  ", rT.std().item<double>(), "exact", 0.01 * std::sqrt((1.0 - std::exp(-2.0 * 0.7 * 2.0)) / (2.0 * 0.7)));
}
```

### Example 2

The second signature: default options with a seed.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace rt = fin::rates;
using pluss::Series;

static double bs(fin::pricing::OptionType type, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price.items<double>()[0];
}
static pluss::Series bsv(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static pluss::Series bst(fin::pricing::OptionType type, const pluss::Series &spots, const pluss::Series &tau, double K, double r, double q, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = {.type = type, .strike = pluss::make_series({K}), .maturity = tau}, .market = {.spot = spots, .rate = pluss::make_series({r}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({q})},
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.price().price;
}
static fin::hedging::DeltaHedgeResult hedge(const pluss::Series &path, fin::pricing::OptionType type, double K, double r, double q, double T, double vol) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(type, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(100.0, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({vol})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic}};
  return fin::hedging::delta_hedge(f, path);
}
static double iv(double price, double S, double K, double r, double q, double T, const fin::pricing::ImpliedVolOptions &o = {}) {
  fin::module::Field f{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, K, T), .market = fin::market::make(S, r, q),
                       .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({0.2})},
                       .controls = {.engine = fin::module::Engine::Analytic, .risk = fin::module::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  return f.implied_vol(pluss::make_series({price}), o).items<double>()[0];
}

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const rt::VasicekParams p{};
  const rt::RatePaths a = rt::vasicek_paths(10, 5, 0.1, p, pluss::Config{}, 7);
  const rt::RatePaths b = rt::vasicek_paths(10, 5, 0.1, p, pluss::Config{}, 7);
  const rt::RatePaths c = rt::vasicek_paths(10, 5, 0.1, p, pluss::Config{}, 8);
  out.writeln("same seed:", (a.rate - b.rate).abs().max().item<double>(), ", other seed:", (a.rate - c.rate).abs().max().item<double>());
}
```

### Example 3

Euler against the exact scheme as the step is refined: the Euler mean converges to the exact one as `dt` shrinks.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <cmath>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace rt = fin::rates;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  const rt::VasicekParams p{.kappa = 1.5, .theta = 0.03, .sigma = 0.01, .r0 = 0.08};
  for (const std::int64_t steps : {2, 8, 64}) {
    rt::SimOptions options;
    options.seed = 3;
    const double mean = rt::vasicek_paths(steps, 100000, 2.0 / steps, p, options).rate.select(0, steps).mean().item<double>();
    out.writeln("steps", steps, ": Euler mean r_2 =", mean, ", exact =", 0.03 + 0.05 * std::exp(-3.0));
  }
}
```

### Example 4

Paths first: the layout transposes.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace rt = fin::rates;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(0));
  rt::SimOptions options;
  options.paths_first = true;
  out.writeln(rt::vasicek_paths(10, 5, 0.1, rt::VasicekParams{}, options).rate.sizes());
}
```

### Example 5

Invalid arguments are refused: a non-positive step count, path count or step.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <string>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace rt = fin::rates;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const rt::VasicekParams p{};
  try {
    (void)(rt::vasicek_paths(0, 10, 0.1, p));
  } catch (const std::exception &e) {
    const std::string text(e.what());
    out.writeln(text.substr(0, text.find('\n')));
  }
  try {
    (void)(rt::vasicek_paths(10, 10, -0.1, p));
  } catch (const std::exception &e) {
    const std::string text(e.what());
    out.writeln(text.substr(0, text.find('\n')));
  }
}
```

